Hi,

A customer asked their card company to reverse a payment they made to
<%= @event.name %>. This is called a dispute, or a chargeback.

While it is being reviewed, <%= render_money @dispute.amount_cents %> has been
taken off what Fuime owes you for that sale. That is why the amount on your
payouts page changed.

You do not need to do anything. Fuime is the legal seller on every sale made
through the platform, so the card company's dispute is with Fuime and we handle
the response. If we win it, the amount goes back to what you are owed. If we
lose it, it stays reduced — that is the part of selling online that we carry
with you.

If you know something about this sale that would help — what you delivered,
when, and any messages with the customer — reply to this email and it will reach
a person. It genuinely helps.

Your payouts page: <%= @payouts_url %>

Questions: <%= @support_email %>
